Vercel Web Analytics Installation Complete

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

Changes Made:
--------------

1. Package Installation
   - Installed @vercel/analytics version 2.0.1
   - Updated package.json with the new dependency
   - Updated package-lock.json with dependency tree

2. Analytics Integration (app/layout.tsx)
   - Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next"`
   - Added <Analytics /> component inside the <body> tag after all providers
   - Placement follows Vercel's official Next.js App Router pattern

Implementation Details:
----------------------
- Followed the latest official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- Used Next.js App Router integration pattern as specified in the docs
- Placed Analytics component at the end of the body to avoid interfering with existing providers (ThemeProvider, MeProvider, I18nProvider)
- Build verification completed successfully - no TypeScript errors or build issues

Files Modified:
--------------
- web/app/layout.tsx - Added Analytics import and component
- web/package.json - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- web/package-lock.json - Updated with new dependency tree

Next Steps:
----------
To activate analytics tracking:
1. Deploy this change to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard for this project
3. Verify tracking is working by checking the browser Network tab for analytics requests after deployment

The implementation is production-ready and follows Vercel's recommended best practices.
